Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:07:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] camera: Restore stock OnePlus extension ABI entry points

Provide the legacy two-argument rotation transform and three-argument camera characteristics overloads by forwarding to the current implementations. Restore CameraThreadState caller IDs with the same Binder/HwBinder transport selection used by AttributionAndPermissionUtils.

Bridge the old capture-result and buffer-return signatures to current helpers. Recover zoom-ratio mode from the live in-flight request, collect and finish real output buffers, and restore the caller-owned in-flight lock after delivering callbacks outside it. These adapters require framework-owned state; they do not recreate or certify Android 12 private class layouts.

Test: compiled the modified ARM64 translation units with existing Android build flags, relinked only the three affected libraries in /tmp with one linker thread, and passed the original complete libcsextimpl check_elf_file invocation. No undefined-symbol allowance, prebuilt modification, full ROM build or device camera validation.
Change-Id: Ie94221aeb8c1ad0dbc9ac6251ba8deb99c4c240b
